# ── Obsidian ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ignore the entire Obsidian config folder. This is the safest
# default: it guarantees that secrets — such as the Local REST API
# key stored in
#   .obsidian/plugins/obsidian-local-rest-api/data.json
# — are never committed to the repository.
#
# If you later decide you want to version some of your Obsidian
# settings, you can selectively un-ignore files here. But NEVER
# un-ignore plugin data files that contain API keys or tokens.
.obsidian/

# Extra safety net: explicitly ignore the Local REST API key file,
# even if parts of .obsidian/ are ever tracked.
.obsidian/plugins/obsidian-local-rest-api/data.json

# Common secret/credential files
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*

# ── MCP / Claude config (may contain API keys in plaintext) ──
# Project-scoped MCP server config and local Claude settings can
# embed bearer tokens (e.g. the Local REST API key). Keep them out
# of version control. If you ever want to share a secret-free
# .mcp.json, use ${ENV_VAR} substitution and un-ignore it.
.mcp.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── OS / editor cruft ─────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.trash/
*.swp
*~
